WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.533
CNN learning

00:00:00.533 --> 00:00:02.702
exclusively about a new CIA campaign.

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:03.670
And this one is aimed

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:04.738
at recruiting Russians

00:00:04.738 --> 00:00:06.573
to spy for the United States.

00:00:06.573 --> 00:00:07.841
Our Alex Marquardt

00:00:07.841 --> 00:00:10.377
obtaining remarkable video from the CIA

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:11.678
with their message

00:00:11.678 --> 00:00:13.079
intended to lure Russians

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:14.748
and turn them against Putin.

00:00:14.748 --> 00:00:16.049
It is a story you'll see.

00:00:16.049 --> 00:00:18.184
First, OUTFRONT

00:00:18.718 --> 00:00:19.252
will

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:22.856
at the television shattering image, tough

00:00:23.823 --> 00:00:26.059
to beat, notoriously difficult

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:28.561
questions being asked in Russian.

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:30.030
And a new dramatic video

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:31.264
by the CIA

00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:32.966
just released to try to recruit

00:00:32.966 --> 00:00:34.467
more Russian spies

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:35.702
by appealing to Russians

00:00:35.702 --> 00:00:37.704
patriotism, frustrations

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:38.972
and the oppression they face.

00:00:38.972 --> 00:00:41.374
Under the Putin regime.

00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:44.077
CIA officials told CNN

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:45.512
in an exclusive interview

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:46.813
that the war in Ukraine

00:00:46.813 --> 00:00:49.516
has created an unprecedented opportunity

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:50.750
that they want to capitalize

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:52.986
on to recruit new Russian assets.

00:00:52.986 --> 00:00:54.421
Disaffection with the war

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:55.188
will continue

00:00:55.188 --> 00:00:57.390
to nor away at the Russian leadership.

00:00:57.757 --> 00:00:59.492
Beneath the steady diet of state

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:01.761
propaganda and practiced repression

00:01:01.995 --> 00:01:03.830
in the past year of the war,

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:06.032
the CIA has been encouraging Russians

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:07.567
with valuable information

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:10.103
to contact them quietly, securely

00:01:10.103 --> 00:01:11.504
and anonymously

00:01:11.504 --> 00:01:13.473
through a portal on the dark web.

00:01:13.473 --> 00:01:15.241
We're looking around the world

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:16.643
for Russians

00:01:16.643 --> 00:01:19.579
who are is disgusted with that is we are

00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:21.047
because we're open for business.

00:01:21.047 --> 00:01:22.615
Instructions have been posted

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:24.918
on the CIA's social media accounts.

00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:26.252
And this new video,

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:28.154
after making an emotional pitch

00:01:28.154 --> 00:01:29.255
to Russian viewers.

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:31.024
Details how to do that

00:01:31.024 --> 00:01:33.393
using the dark web browser called Tor.

00:01:33.426 --> 00:01:34.761
You're not powerless.

00:01:34.761 --> 00:01:37.263
It says Contact us in a safe way.

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:39.065
The CIA recruitment video

00:01:39.065 --> 00:01:40.033
was first posted

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:41.601
Monday evening on Telegram.

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:42.802
The social media app

00:01:42.802 --> 00:01:44.838
that is highly popular among Russians

00:01:44.838 --> 00:01:46.439
who can't easily access

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:47.474
unfiltered news

00:01:47.474 --> 00:01:49.809
or other social media sites that call it

00:01:49.976 --> 00:01:51.945
hanging out the shingle

00:01:51.945 --> 00:01:53.580
and spreading the word far and wide

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:54.781
that U.S.

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:55.748
and counterintelligence

00:01:55.748 --> 00:01:57.750
is open for business.

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.319
And we have deep pockets

00:01:59.319 --> 00:02:00.420
and we want to strike

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:01.521
back against this man.

00:02:01.521 --> 00:02:03.656
You hate Vladimir Putin.

00:02:03.656 --> 00:02:05.191
You have an opportunity now to do it

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:05.758
safely.

00:02:05.758 --> 00:02:07.961
CIA officials told CNN they hope

00:02:07.961 --> 00:02:09.062
the video will resonate

00:02:09.062 --> 00:02:10.430
beyond intelligence

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:11.598
and security officials

00:02:11.598 --> 00:02:12.132
with people

00:02:12.132 --> 00:02:13.166
who may not realize

00:02:13.166 --> 00:02:14.934
that they have sensitive information

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:16.903
to share working, for example,

00:02:16.903 --> 00:02:19.672
in cyber tech, finance and other fields.

00:02:19.706 --> 00:02:21.708
They may think contacting the CIA

00:02:21.708 --> 00:02:23.776
is too difficult or too dangerous.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:25.378
The CIA telling CNN

00:02:25.378 --> 00:02:27.247
they want to demystify that.

00:02:27.247 --> 00:02:27.914
We need people

00:02:27.914 --> 00:02:30.517
all through the Russian economy

00:02:30.917 --> 00:02:31.951
to cooperate with us.

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:33.953
We need to know what's going on

00:02:33.953 --> 00:02:35.588
in this adversary country.

00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:38.424
There is no direct mention

00:02:38.424 --> 00:02:39.025
of Putin

00:02:39.025 --> 00:02:41.995
or Ukraine, nor CIA officials insist.

00:02:42.162 --> 00:02:44.497
Is it meant to fuel unrest in Russia?

00:02:44.531 --> 00:02:45.932
Rather, they tell CNN

00:02:45.932 --> 00:02:47.567
these are timeless themes

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:48.101
that they hope

00:02:48.101 --> 00:02:49.202
will drive Russians

00:02:49.202 --> 00:02:51.571
into the arms of the CIA

00:02:51.571 --> 00:02:53.673
at the double get money out of Syria.

00:02:55.375 --> 00:02:56.776
Every state

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:59.612
messenger, every state

00:02:59.913 --> 00:03:01.447
read the story.

00:03:01.447 --> 00:03:02.148
A good idea.

00:03:02.148 --> 00:03:03.650
My name is

00:03:06.052 --> 00:03:06.753
in terms of what

00:03:06.753 --> 00:03:08.288
the CIA has already seen

00:03:08.288 --> 00:03:09.355
and their efforts to recruit

00:03:09.355 --> 00:03:11.491
new Russian spies during this war.

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:13.293
They say they have been successful.

00:03:13.293 --> 00:03:15.662
One CIA official told me, in his words,

00:03:15.962 --> 00:03:18.231
there's contact coming in now, Aaron.

00:03:18.231 --> 00:03:19.632
They won't give any numbers

00:03:19.632 --> 00:03:21.334
or say where these Russians work,

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:22.202
but the CIA says

00:03:22.202 --> 00:03:22.635
they wouldn't

00:03:22.635 --> 00:03:24.204
be rolling out this new video

00:03:24.204 --> 00:03:26.539
if they hadn't already had some success.

00:03:26.673 --> 00:03:27.307
We should also note

00:03:27.307 --> 00:03:29.042
that the FBI has tried

00:03:29.042 --> 00:03:30.043
recruiting Russian spies

00:03:30.043 --> 00:03:31.244
right here in Washington

00:03:31.244 --> 00:03:31.844
with ads

00:03:31.844 --> 00:03:33.780
specifically targeted at people

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:35.248
coming and going

00:03:35.248 --> 00:03:36.883
from the Russian embassy,

00:03:36.883 --> 00:03:38.551
an effort that the embassy called

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:40.286
ridiculous Aaron.

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:42.355
Alex, thank you very much.

00:03:42.355 --> 00:03:43.690
It is important in that context, though,

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:44.490
just a note to everybody.

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:45.291
There are a lot of

00:03:46.359 --> 00:03:47.393
Russians who are coming and

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:48.962
going out of the United States

00:03:48.962 --> 00:03:50.697
that that is still the reality.

00:03:50.697 --> 00:03:50.930
All right.

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:52.498
OUTFRONT now, Elina Polyakov, us,

00:03:52.498 --> 00:03:54.267
she is a Russian foreign affairs expert

00:03:54.267 --> 00:03:54.968
and the president

00:03:54.968 --> 00:03:56.703
and CEO of the Center for European

00:03:56.703 --> 00:03:58.471
Policy Analysis.

00:03:58.471 --> 00:03:59.005
So, Elina,

00:03:59.005 --> 00:04:02.041
as you hear these recruitment videos,

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:02.809
which just to be clear,

00:04:02.809 --> 00:04:03.743
are going out on Telegram

00:04:03.743 --> 00:04:05.211
as Alex is reporting.

00:04:05.211 --> 00:04:06.279
That is a place

00:04:06.279 --> 00:04:08.248
where Russians spend a lot of time.

00:04:08.248 --> 00:04:09.482
That is the social media,

00:04:09.482 --> 00:04:11.784
the predominant social media in Russia.

00:04:12.018 --> 00:04:13.853
So what do you hear

00:04:13.853 --> 00:04:15.288
when you hear these videos

00:04:15.288 --> 00:04:16.222
and the appeal

00:04:16.222 --> 00:04:17.523
that they're making to retain

00:04:17.523 --> 00:04:18.091
your dignity,

00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:20.693
to take care of your family?

00:04:20.994 --> 00:04:23.263
I mean, hearing the Russian language

00:04:23.263 --> 00:04:25.531
is being spoken in these videos just now,

00:04:25.832 --> 00:04:27.300
I think it's absolutely brilliant.

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:29.135
Honestly, there are so many Russians

00:04:29.135 --> 00:04:30.737
that we will never, ever hear from

00:04:31.704 --> 00:04:33.640
who are disappointed

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:34.440
with the future

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:35.341
they see ahead of them,

00:04:35.341 --> 00:04:37.076
which is a very, very bleak future

00:04:37.076 --> 00:04:38.511
under President Putin.

00:04:38.511 --> 00:04:39.512
And we'll never hear them

00:04:39.512 --> 00:04:40.713
talk about this publicly

00:04:40.713 --> 00:04:42.048
because people in Russia

00:04:42.048 --> 00:04:44.250
are really deeply afraid

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:45.451
of the kind of punishment

00:04:45.451 --> 00:04:46.386
that might come with saying

00:04:46.386 --> 00:04:47.453
anything in public.

00:04:47.453 --> 00:04:48.121
You know, let's remember,

00:04:48.121 --> 00:04:48.855
this is a country

00:04:48.855 --> 00:04:50.323
that will throw you in jail

00:04:50.323 --> 00:04:52.458
for holding up a white sheet of paper

00:04:52.558 --> 00:04:53.693
with no words on it.

00:04:53.693 --> 00:04:56.462
So I think this is an absolutely

00:04:56.763 --> 00:04:58.965
brilliant ploy by the CIA

00:04:58.998 --> 00:05:01.834
to see if we can get some informants

00:05:02.602 --> 00:05:03.836
average people

00:05:03.836 --> 00:05:05.605
to cooperate with the United States.

00:05:05.605 --> 00:05:06.105
Now, Olena,

00:05:06.105 --> 00:05:07.240
you heard what Alex is reporting.

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:08.841
He's saying the CIA knows that

00:05:08.841 --> 00:05:09.242
in a sense

00:05:09.242 --> 00:05:10.443
that they return on investment,

00:05:10.443 --> 00:05:11.210
that they're doing this

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:11.944
because they

00:05:11.944 --> 00:05:14.080
